# Local audit / self-review working artifacts — generated on-machine, never committed.
# On case-insensitive filesystems (macOS) Docs/ collides with docs/, so the
# earlier `!docs/**` negation would otherwise re-include these — re-ignore both
# casings explicitly by path.
Docs/routing-audit-agent/
docs/routing-audit-agent/
Docs/self-audit-loop/
docs/self-audit-loop/
Docs/AUDIT_PROMPT_*.md

# Re-ignore OS junk under Docs/ — the earlier `!docs/**` negation un-ignores it
**/.DS_Store

# Internal business/enterprise-evaluation docs — never publish to the public repo
docs-private/

# Audit evidence: sqlite SNAPSHOTS only (two 61M usage.db captures from RED2's
# unknown-vs-zero reproduction). The audit DOCUMENTS are tracked — see
# .chuzom/zero-tolerance-audit/ — because G-C grades work against criteria in
# them and an untracked oracle is one the executor can silently edit. The
# snapshots are excluded for size alone; their sha256 is recorded in
# CRITERIA_MANIFEST.sha256 so their integrity is still checkable.
.chuzom/zero-tolerance-audit/evidence/**/*.db
.chuzom/zero-tolerance-audit/evidence/**/*.db-shm
.chuzom/zero-tolerance-audit/evidence/**/*.db-wal

# G-F working run artefacts (scripts/gf_mutmut.py --out). Deliberately IGNORED:
# G-C's hash manifest covers .chuzom/zero-tolerance-audit/ only, so anything
# committed here would look like audit evidence while being unsealed. The
# artefacts that must be tamper-evident — the universe manifest, the seed inputs
# and the holdout hash — go under .chuzom/zero-tolerance-audit/ in Phase 1,
# where the seal actually applies.
.chuzom/gf/
